// The unattended run (M2 design §19.6): the default world as generated, but
// its 30 first sprites are newborns, placed as the Cursor places them and
// spread over the whole map, and nobody else is there, so no young sprite
// has anyone to learn from. Each grows up or dies within about 5,000 ticks.
// A4 (design §7.4) and G5 (M2 design §6) ask that 10% to 30% grow up, in
// the middle seed of ten. Baseline runs use it on seeds 1–10:
// cargo run --release -p terra-sim --example lab -- scenarios/unattended.ron --seeds 10
(
    world: Unattended,
    ticks: 6000,
    windows: [(0, 6000)],
)
